-- APPLY-0175.sql - paste into the Supabase SQL editor (STAGING first; production only when the owner says go).
-- Run AFTER APPLY-0171.sql. Trial studios: the owner's 3 layout templates (adds the sofa-lounge reception, archives the theatre sample; never deletes). Safe to run twice.
begin;
-- 0175_trial_layout_templates.sql - CANONICAL forward-only. REQUIRES 0096 + 0169 (+ 0171 for the manifest).
--
-- In plain words:
--   Free-trial studios should see exactly the owner's 3 layouts as templates:
--     1  Wedding   - Grand Lawn (450+ guests)            (0169, unchanged)
--     2  Corporate - Round tables gala (120 guests)      (0169, unchanged)
--     3  Reception - Lawn reception with sofa lounge     (NEW here, from the owner's 3rd layout file)
--   The 0169 "Corporate - Theatre/conference" sample template is ARCHIVED (never deleted) in the
--   sample master and in existing trial studios, only while it still carries its original 0169 name.
--   Existing trial studios also get template 3 once (by name). Paid studios are never touched
--   (only studios whose subscription status is trial right now, or the sample master; converted paid studios keep trial_ends_at so it is NOT used). A new manifest is published
--   once so new trials get the set. Nothing is deleted. ASCII only. Safe to run twice.
-- ============================================================================

do $$ begin
  if to_regclass('public.studio_layout_templates') is null then
    raise exception '0175 needs 0096 + 0169 first'; end if;
end $$;

